efinition. This is usually a list of numbers or labels, typically in ~~
some unit of time (days, weeks, months, etc.).  Use the “Dynamic()” f~~
unction in your variables to perform dynamic simulation.Samplesize := 1000Typechecking := 1Checking := 1Saveoptions := 2Savevalues := 0Allwarnings := 0Model Earthquake_expenseTitle: Earthquake expense riskDescription: An example of risk analysis with time-dependence and cost~~
s of events shifted over time.   ~
~
Assume (for example):~
* Earthquakes are Poisson events with a mean rate of once every 10 ye~~
ars.~
* Damage caused by such a quake is lognormally distributed with a mea~~
n of $10M and a standard deviation of $6M.~
* Cost of damage gets incurred over the period of a year from the dat~~
e of the quake as equipment is replaced, adn building are repaired ov~~
er time:~
   - 20% in the 1st quarter following quake~
   - 50% in 2nd quarter~
   - 20% in 3rd quarter~
   - 10% in 4th quarter~
~
Answer questions like:~
* What is the likelihood of more than one quake in a specific 10 year~~
 period.~
* For any number of seleted time windows (say quarter 3 of year 21):~
  - Distribution of expected costs (mean, std.dev, etc)~
  - Probability that in that time window my costs exceed $X?~
Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
